\cf2 I am not at all sure the people interpreted the riddle the way we do, having been given the interpretation. Not only might they have been considering alternative interpretations, they might have paused at confusion. This is not exactly an easy interpretation to arrive at, either intellectually or spiritually. Intellectually, while there are clear connections in the riddle with its interpretation between the all devouring nature of fire and sword, this was not at all a standard pairing, so the meaning may have been unclear given just the riddle. Spiritually, we know from the rest of Ezekiel that the exiles were rebellious, and needed the indirection of riddle and the forcefulness of an interpretation such as this one to reach them despite their stony hearts. \
