The structural question becomes more complex when we consider the audience's state. If they were genuinely confused by the riddle rather than just dismissive, then the interpretation doesn't just clarify - it confronts them with something they couldn't have imagined. The shift from riddle to interpretation to embodied groaning might trace their journey from confusion through horrified understanding to physical collapse.\
The groaning that prompts the question in verse 12 - this isn't just about the content of the message but about what happens when someone truly comprehends it. The physical symptoms Ezekiel describes (melting hearts, slack hands, fainting spirits, watery knees) suggest the body's response when the mind can't deflect anymore.\
