\cf2 Your point about the exiles' physical reaction being response to "the holiness and sovereignty of the revealed LORD" rather than just earthly disaster is crucial. The melting, slackening, fainting, and liquefying aren't just fear but recognition of creatureliness before absolute holiness. This connects to Isaiah 6's "Woe is me, I am undone" - the body's collapse when deflection mechanisms fail.\
