Verse 13 (English) is grammatically difficult at best, that is, we have to make some grammatical and interpretational choices. Some of those choices are easier than others.\
For instance, grammatical gender is a guide here. Despises is feminine, as is sword, so the subject of despises is sword. Similarly, be is masculine, as is scepter, so the subject of scepter is masculine. \
Other choices are harder. For instance, it is entirely legal to insert it is, before testing. Skipping such words is entirely normal in Hebrew. But neither are we required to read it that way. Perhaps we should prefer the more coherent alternative.\
